# Test: a forked plugin reads the ze keys the daemon was started with, in the
# dotted spelling and with a hyphen in the key (spec-plugin-fork-environment).
# VALIDATES: the daemon's own environment holds ze.test.fork.environment.dotted
#            (dotted) and ze.test.fork-environment.hyphen-key (dotted and
#            hyphenated). The observer runs as a forked plugin, started by
#            (*Process).startExternal through /bin/sh -c, and reads both keys
#            with env.Get from its own process environment. Nothing else in
#            the daemon reads these keys or sends them to the plugin, so its
#            OK line proves both crossed the shell into the child.
# PREVENTS: startExternal handing the child the daemon's environment as it
#           is. dash drops every variable whose name is not a shell
#           identifier, so a dotted key never reached a forked plugin, and a
#           hyphenated key had no spelling that did: the plugin read the
#           key's default and said nothing.
#
# DISCRIMINATION: replacing env.ShellSafe(os.Environ()) with os.Environ() in
# startExternal (internal/component/plugin/process/process.go) turns this
# red: the observer reads both keys as "" and fails, naming the key.
#
# An earlier draft asserted the as-path filter decision lines instead. Those
# are written by the match reporter in the daemon (policychain), which reads
# the daemon's own dotted keys, so it stayed green with the fix removed.

option=env:var=ze.test.fork.environment.dotted:value=dotted
option=env:var=ze.test.fork-environment.hyphen-key:value=hyphen
option=timeout:value=30s

stdin=ze-conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
plugin {
	external fork-environment {
		run "le test fixture plugin/fork-environment"
		encoder json
	}
}
policy {
	prefix-list CUSTOMERS {
		entry 10.0.0.0/8 {
			ge 16
			le 24
			action accept
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze -:stdin=ze-conf:timeout=30s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:contains=OK: the forked plugin read ze.test.fork.environment.dotted=dotted ze.test.fork-environment.hyphen-key=hyphen
reject=stderr:pattern=did not reach it through the shell
reject=stderr:pattern=ZE-OBSERVER-FAIL
reject=stderr:pattern=panic recovered
reject=stderr:pattern=fatal error
